level0	2269	MonoBehaviour			20887633920	level1atext	"Emily's heart pounded in her chest as she watched the figure in the shadows. She knew that she had to act quickly before he made a move. She grabbed her phone and dialed 911. ""The killer is outside my safe house,"" she said, her voice shaking. ""Please, you have to help me."" The operator assured her that help was on the way, but Emily knew that she couldn't wait. She needed to protect herself. She looked around the room and saw a fireplace poker. It wasn't much, but it was better than nothing. Emily approached the door, the poker in her hand. She could hear footsteps approaching, and her heart raced as she waited for the killer to burst through the door. Suddenly, the door burst open, and the killer lunged at her with a knife. Emily swung the poker, hitting him in the face. He stumbled back, but he didn't fall. He lunged at her again, but this time, Emily was ready. She swung the poker again, hitting him in the side of the head. He fell to the ground, unconscious. "
